+
+## The log
+
+One line per record: the time to the millisecond, the stage, a one-line summary. Click a line for the raw data: Whisper’s raw text (each guess, each amendment, the final), each send, Servex writing it, each reply, each placement, each error with its stack. The last 200 records are kept (`DictateHealth.KEEP`). **Copy report** puts every light and record on the clipboard as JSON; beside it, the session log, the Whisper log and the failures file.
+
+## The handle
+
+In the phone sheet, the Debug panel sits under the chat. A handle on its top edge resizes it: drag it up for more log, down for more chat (a sheet within a sheet). Its height is saved on this device (`localStorage`, `lew42.sheet.tabs_h`), so it survives a reload; a double-click puts the default back (`Sheet.Panel.tabs_grip`, [ext/drawer/Sheet.js](/framework/ext/drawer/Sheet.js)).
+
+## Every error caught
+
+Each stage catches its errors and either shows them (a red light and a log line, with the raw error) or ignores them on purpose, with a one-line comment in the code saying why. `DictateHealth.fail(stage, error, where)` is the one way to show one. What changed on 2026-10-25 (`test/errors.mjs`):
+- **One bad line no longer freezes the chat.** `Session.watch` caught everything around the whole poll, so a line that failed to draw stopped the rest and was retried every 1.5 s, forever, in silence. Now each line is drawn on its own, a failure is on the Page light, and the poll’s own failures (and recovery) are on the Wire light. A half-written last line is read again on the next poll instead of being skipped.
+- Errors that went only to the console now light their stage: the sentence queue, the pause that sends, a deliver that threw, a guess request, the fallback log refusing the words, a failed poll or a half-bad session log.
+- Deliberately ignored, each with its reason in a one-line comment beside it: the check or ? mark on a bubble (a bonus), a suspended audio context that cannot resume (shows as no sound), the Whisper log copy (the Debug log holds the answer), a start's own failure shown once by `start()`.
+
+## Reconnect
+
+The sheet’s Reconnect reopens one thing: the chat’s live wire to Servex, the Wire light. It shows only after that wire has been down 8 s, saying for how long and why, and a press never throws or opens a second wire. Details: [ext/drawer/doc/sheet.md](/framework/ext/drawer/doc/sheet.md#reconnect-2026-10-25).
 
